WEBVTT

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.611
spanning millions of years.

00:04:01.237 --> 00:04:04.949
We were donated wood samples
from almost every country:

00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:06.367
the Indian Banyan,

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:07.368
the White Mulberry,

00:04:07.368 --> 00:04:08.869
the Dawn Redwood

00:04:08.869 --> 00:04:11.455
and twigs from sacred forests around us.

00:04:12.039 --> 00:04:13.874
Looking upwards into the light,

00:04:13.874 --> 00:04:16.711
we see the most threatened
tree species of now.

00:04:18.421 --> 00:04:19.922
More recently in my practice,

00:04:19.922 --> 00:04:24.552
I’ve come to believe that looking forward
is just as important as looking back.

00:04:25.428 --> 00:04:27.680
How do we speak to unborn people?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.391
How do we build a bridge across time?